<topic template="Default" status="Under Construction" modified="2025-04-09T12:32:33.526-04:00" lasteditedby="rbwinst" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../helpproject.xsd">
  <title translate="true">ESL: GWE Energy Source Loading Package</title>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1"><text styleclass="Heading1" translate="true">ESL: GWE Energy Source Loading Package</text></para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">The </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">ESL: GWE Energy Source Loading Package</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> pane is on the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="MODFLOW_Features_Tab" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">MODFLOW Features</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> tab of the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="Object_Properties_Dialog_Box" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Object Properties</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> dialog box.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">The data that can be specified for the ESL package are the </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Starting time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">, </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Ending time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">, </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source Active</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">, </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source, Energy Source Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true"> and the </text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Chemical Species</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">. However, the Chemical Species is always set to &quot;Temperature.&quot;</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">The </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true"> is the energy source loading rate for the selected </text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Chemical Species</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> (which is always &quot;Temperataure&quot;)</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">. A positive value indicates addition of energy and a negative value indicates removal of energy. If SI units are used for the model, the units of energy are Joules. If other unit are used in the model, the units of energy should be adjusted appropriately.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Active</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:normal;" translate="true">&quot; can be used to turn on or off a ESL boundary. If the formula for </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Active</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> evaluates to True, a energy source loading loading boundary will be defined. If it evaluates to False, a energy source loading boundary will not be defined. This can be used to turn on or off energy source loading boundaries at different locations based on a criterion specified by the user. Such a capability can be useful for specifying tidal boundaries where some locations may be alternately flooded or exposed.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> is only used if it has been activated in the</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true">&#32;</text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="ESL-GWE-Energy-Source-Loading" styleclass="Strong" translate="true">ESL: GWE Energy Source Loading Package</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">. If </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> is specified, the concentration is multiplied by the </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Energy Source</text><text styleclass="Strong" translate="true"> Multiplier</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> value.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Starting time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> and </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Ending time</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> are explained in the help for the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="MODFLOW_Features_Tab" anchor="Times" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">MODFLOW Features</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> tab.</text></para>
  </body>
</topic>
